course: dictionary
lesson: 980
title: Boasting and being modest
level: primary-4
stars: 1
explain: To boast means to talk too proudly about yourself, what you have or what you can do. «In the playground, boasts fly like footballs.» Picture those proud words flying around fast and bumping into everyone. That is how boasting spreads.
explain: Boast can also mean to have something good that you are proud of. «The town boasts a big park» means the town has a park it is proud of. Look at the words around boast to tell which meaning the writer uses.
explain: Being modest means not showing off, and it is kind. Boasting can upset others and push friends away, but sharing the fun brings friends closer. In fables, the boastful hare in The Tortoise and the Hare often loses.
fact: A boast is a proud statement about yourself.
fact: To boast means to talk too proudly about yourself, your things or your skills.
fact: «The town boasts a big park» means the town has a park it is proud of.
fact: Boasting about having more than others makes them feel small and pushes friends away.
fact: Wise people can stop a boast without shaming the boaster.
exercise: What do the boasts mean in «In the playground, boasts fly like footballs»? | Gifts given to friends | Quiet whispers between friends | *Proud talk about yourself | A kind of football game
exercise: «The school boasts a big garden.» What does boasts mean here? | Moves the garden to another place | Hides its garden away from visitors | *Has something good that it is proud of | Talks too proudly about itself
exercise: Which friend is most likely to make others feel small? | Omar, who shares his lunch with a friend | Priya, who passes the ball to her team | Ruth, who says well done to others | *Sam, who keeps telling everyone he is better than them
test:  Which word means to talk too proudly about yourself? | Gentle | Whisper | *Boast | Modest
test:  What often happens to the boastful hare in a fable? | He is given a prize for being kind | He always wins the race | *He often loses | He becomes a king
exam:  Ella says, «Boasting helps me make friends.» Is she right? | *No, boasting makes others feel small and pushes friends away | Yes, everyone loves a show-off | No, because boasting means whispering quietly | Yes, because boasting is always kind
